Aishi & Reimu (SAGE '25 Demo) for AmigaOS 3 - @RELEASE_VERSION@
============================================================

The Amiga OpenSurge engine, ready to play Aishi & Reimu (SAGE '25 Demo),
a fan game made with the Open Surge Engine. No separate engine install is
needed.

THIS ARCHIVE HAS NONE OF THE GAME'S OWN FILES. Its makers have not said
they may be passed on, so they are not. Download the game yourself, from
its page:

  https://sonicfangameshq.com/forums/showcase/aishi-reimu-sage-25-demo.2638/

  file     Aishi & Reimu (SAGE '25 Demo).zip
  size     163830376 bytes
  sha256   3f80a6fea4cb790fd0e0d5090565e8f111f3eb42c6c9d9ccd5ab29432277fd51

The game, its characters and its music belong to their makers and owners;
it is not made by or for SEGA, or by Team Shanghai Alice.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install-AishiReimu beside the AishiReimu drawer. It checks the
CPU,
FPU and GFOpenGPU, asks where the AishiReimu drawer should go (Work:Games is
offered), copies the engine there, and then asks for the game you
downloaded:

- the archive itself: the Installer checks its size and unpacks it with
  SYS:Utilities/GFOpenCompress (part of AmiCradle) into the drawer;
- or the folder "Aishi & Reimu (SAGE '25 Demo)" that unpacking it made;
- or a game.zip made from the download on another computer with the port's
  scripts/prepare-amiga-port.sh.

It checks the folder's name and the sizes of a few of its files, then
copies the game's files into AishiReimu/Game, leaving out the Windows
program
files. Running Install-AishiReimu again replaces or keeps those files.

A computer with a shell can check the download's SHA-256 first:
  sha256sum "Aishi & Reimu (SAGE '25 Demo).zip"

What is in the drawer
---------------------
StartGame   starts the game (once its files are installed)
Engine/     the OpenSurge engine (below)
Game/       the game's own files, from your download (Install-AishiReimu)
Tools/      what Install-AishiReimu uses
Licences/   licences and the engine's source

What it needs
-------------
- AmigaOS 3.2 (Installer 43.3 or newer for Install-AishiReimu)
- a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU
- GFOpenGPU: LIBS:GFOpenGPU/GL.module and SDL2.module (as on AmiCradle)
- about 560 MB free on the hard disk, and plenty of Fast RAM

The engine
----------
Engine/ is Amiga OpenSurge, Open Surge Engine 0.6.1.3 for AmigaOS 3,
exactly as released:

  release   @ENGINE_REPO@ @ENGINE_TAG@
  commit    @ENGINE_COMMIT@
  archive   @ENGINE_ASSET@
  sha256    @ENGINE_SHA256@
  program   Engine/opensurge
  sha256    @ENGINE_BINARY_SHA256@
  compiler  @ENGINE_COMPILER@

No separate engine install is needed: StartGame runs this copy. The engine
keeps its settings (surge.prefs), logfile.txt and the game's compatibility
pack in the Game drawer when the game was installed from your download, or
in Engine/.userdata with a game.zip. Licences/SOURCE.txt says where its
source is.

Starting and playing
--------------------
Double-click StartGame in the AishiReimu drawer. From a Shell, CD to the
drawer first, then Execute StartGame. F10 switches between a window and
the full screen. Leave the game from its own menu (Esc brings it up in
most games).

